---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const pageUrl = (path) => `${base}${path}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Career — Anirudh Bompada"
  description="Anirudh Bompada's data-engineering work across Databricks, PySpark, and Azure."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Career</p>
    <h1>Building dependable <span class="accent">data platforms.</span></h1>
    <p class="page-intro">
      I work in data engineering, with an increasing focus on Databricks and the platform
      capabilities behind reliable pipelines and day-to-day operations.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-grid">
    <aside>
      <p>FOCUS / DATABRICKS</p>
      <p>TOOLS / PYTHON + SQL</p>
      <p>DOMAIN / DATA ENGINEERING</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Data pipelines and cloud platforms</h2>
      <p>
        My work has involved building data ingestion and transformation pipelines with
        Python, SQL, Spark, and Azure services. I have also worked with Terraform and
        deployment automation to support the infrastructure those pipelines need.
      </p>

      <h2>A stronger Databricks focus</h2>
      <p>
        More recently, similar data-engineering work has given me more room to focus on
        Databricks itself: its capabilities, how they support data workflows, and how to
        use the platform effectively as requirements evolve.
      </p>

      <h2>How I approach the work</h2>
      <p>
        I like to understand the path from a data source to a usable result, including
        testing, code review, deployment, and the ongoing maintenance of the platform.
      </p>

      <h2>Independent technical work</h2>
      <p>
        Outside my professional work, I run local language-model tests as an independent
        technical project. The benchmarks are separate from any workplace systems.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={pageUrl('projects/llm-benchmark')}>
        Explore my LLM benchmark testing
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
